1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,280
The tower of london the perfect place to start today's walk.
伦敦塔，是开始今天这趟散步的理想地点。

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:14,720
A journey into london's deep past a walk through time.
一段深入伦敦往昔的旅程，一次穿越时间的漫步。

3
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:23,399
So today we're going to go for a walk through chuda london using this map of london in 1520.
今天我们要用这张1520年的伦敦地图，走进都铎时代的伦敦（字幕作chuda）。

4
00:00:23,399 --> 00:00:29,640
This is the map I picked up at one of the buildings that would have been in london in 1520.
我在一栋1520年就已存在于伦敦的建筑里拿到了这张地图。

5
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,800
Um the charter house there the charter house museum.
嗯，就是Charterhouse，那里的Charterhouse博物馆。

6
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:37,079
So before I get going I highly recommend that you go along to the ch house museum and pick up this beautiful map.
出发前，我强烈建议感兴趣的人去那家博物馆，拿一张这样的漂亮地图。

7
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:39,880
If you're interested in it they've also got the map of medieval london.
如果你感兴趣，他们还有中世纪伦敦的地图。

8
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,589
And it's a it's a really beautiful reconstruction it as it says in its text.
那是一份非常漂亮的复原图，正如它的说明文字所说。

9
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:51,800
It's a reconstruction of a city that no longer exists a city that has vanished.
它复原的是一座已不复存在、已经消失的城市。

10
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:58,559
But has it has it vanished we're going to walk through some of the surviving areas of chuda london.
但它真的消失了吗？我们会走过一些都铎伦敦仍然留存的地方。

11
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:06,120
Or look for some of the remnants or the echoes of the london of Henry the 8 the london of thomas cromwell.
或者寻找亨利八世、托马斯·克伦威尔时代伦敦的残迹和回声。

12
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:12,150
If you've been binge watching wolf hall like I have which is partly the inspiration for today's walk.
如果你也像我一样连着看《狼厅》：这也是今天散步的部分灵感来源。

13
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:20,400
So we're starting here at the tower of london which is one of the buildings that would have been here at the time this map uh was.
我们从伦敦塔这里出发，它是这张地图所描绘的年代就已存在的建筑之一，嗯……

14
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:24,240
Well it's been it's a reconstruction of the city but this is one of the buildings that would have existed.
或者说，这张图是对城市的复原，但这确实是当时就存在的一栋建筑。

15
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,920
At that time that is still here there are a number of others.
它直到今天还在；此外还有好几处。

16
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:37,680
And we will take some of those in whilst also looking at the footprints of some of the more significant buildings that were here.
我们会看其中一些，也会看看当时那些更重要建筑留下的基址或痕迹。

17
00:01:38,639 --> 00:01:44,040
Oh this is one of the things with having a map in a windy city like london.
哦，在伦敦这样多风的城市拿着地图，就是会碰到这种事。

18
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:50,080
So we're down here at the tower of london and this is just half that this is the bottom half here.
我们在这里的伦敦塔；这只是半张，这里是下半部分。

19
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:58,440
What's interesting is the amount of the city of london that was own or controlled by religious buildings.
有意思的是，当时伦敦城有多大面积由宗教建筑占有或控制。

20
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:05,879
Of course this is pre reformation of the church of course so by say 1560 1580 this map would have looked very different.
当然，那是在教会改革之前，所以到了例如1560年或1580年，这张地图看起来就会很不一样。

21
00:02:05,879 --> 00:02:12,600
But the the pink and the pale pink buildings are religious buildings of some description or another.
那些粉红色和浅粉红色的建筑，都是某种宗教建筑。

22
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:24,870
Some of them obviously are churches some of them are arms houses or the residences of bishops or other church type prophecies.
其中一些显然是教堂，有些是字幕作arms houses的建筑，或主教住所及其他教会相关地产（后几词识别待复核）。

23
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:36,079
Le leper hospitals etc so I thought what we would do to start is make our way from uh the obvious land m tower of london.
还有麻风病院等等。我想，我们先从那座明显的地标——伦敦塔走起；字幕land m识别不完整。

24
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:47,920
Which is just over there and then I thought we would go up here to cred fires up sething lane which is interesting.
塔就在那边，接着我想我们沿这条路往上，到字幕作cred fires和sething lane的地方；很有意思。

25
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:59,470
The names you know you can recognize them this is uh uh seen lane up sething lane and then we would go to crutched friars.
这些名字，你还能认出来。这条路，字幕作seen lane、sething lane，接着就去Crutched Friars。

26
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:08,960
What a great name and then we'll work our way from there through I think we'll use it we've got the the halls the livery halls which um some of them were in existence.
名字真棒！然后从那里往前走，我想可以看看那些同业公会会馆，其中有些已经存在。

27
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:12,560
On the same site in 1520.
在1520年时，它们就在同一个地点。

28
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:20,640
Some of them were about to profit from the dissolution of the monasteries in the uh coming years but not yet at this point.
有些会在接下来几年里从解散修道院中受益，不过在地图这个时间点还没有。

29
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:27,920
And of course the wonderful all hallows by the tower barking was was here in 1520 as well.
当然，精彩的All Hallows by the Tower，这里提到Barking的这座教堂，在1520年也已经存在。

30
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:36,240
In fact this building here it's on the site of some of the oldest u kind of built fabric in the whole of london.
事实上，这栋建筑的位置保存着伦敦一些最古老的建筑实体。

31
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:46,840
Some anglo saxon masonry still on this site and of course all hallows by the tower brings up the point that they make in the map.
这里仍有一些盎格鲁撒克逊时期的砌体；而这座教堂也引出了地图中提到的一点。

32
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:52,639
There's a wonderful text that comes with the map which is where a lot of my information is going to be coming from today.
地图附有一段很好的说明文字，今天我的许多信息都会来自那里。

33
00:03:52,639 --> 00:03:59,040
So all credit to the uh the historic towns association I'll put the information below.
所以要感谢字幕所说的Historic Towns Association，我会把相关信息放在下面。

34
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:07,240
But they say that the street plan of chuda london owed more to the anglo saxon city than it did the roman city.
但他们说，都铎伦敦的街道布局，更多承袭自盎格鲁撒克逊城市，而非罗马城市。

35
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:11,400
That was the street plan that the chudah city was laid out.
那就是后来都铎城市据以布局的街道格局……
